<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Otto I, Duke of Brunswick-Göttingen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1330–<a href="/years/1394">1394</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Otto the Bad, Otto der Quade</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Otto I, known as Otto the Bad, was Duke of Brunswick-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gottingen">Göttingen</a> from 1367 to 1394. He spent his reign in feuds with neighbouring princes, knights and towns, above all his own town of Göttingen, whose citizens stormed the ducal castle in the town in 1387 and defeated his forces. The feuds left his small principality deep in debt and its towns more independent of their duke.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/otto-i-duke-of-brunswick-gottingen.jpg" alt="Otto I, Duke of Brunswick-Göttingen" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photographer Alkibiades · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Otto_der_Quade_001.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
